  {
    "field": "claim.doc",
    "value": "d = 1 universality: every VC-1 class compresses at kernel size one, with no side information. No finiteness, no distinguished member, no chain hypothesis. Twist the class by any member to place ∅ in it; there the VC bound makes co-member points comparable in the membership order, so every label set is a finite chain; anchor at its maximum, reconstruct with interConvention, and transport the scheme back with the same kernels."
  },
